<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Canning, 1st Earl Canning</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1812–1862</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Lord Canning, Earl Canning</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Canning, 1st Earl Canning, was Governor-General of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> from 1856 to 1862 and became the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">Viceroy</a> when the Crown took over from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> in 1858. He governed during the rebellion of 1857, when his refusal to permit indiscriminate reprisals earned him the nickname 'Clemency Canning'. In 1861 his arbitration, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canning-award">Canning Award</a>, confirmed the separation of Zanzibar from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-canning-1st-earl-canning.jpg" alt="Charles Canning, 1st Earl Canning" width="320" height="449" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Jabez Edwin Mayall · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charles_Canning,_1st_Earl_Canning.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
